d flues clear</text><rect x="800" y="790" width="350" height="54" rx="12" fill="#F6E1D6" stroke="#D8CBBB" stroke-width="2"/><text x="975" y="825" font-size="19" font-weight="700" fill="#C85A32" text-anchor="middle">Converting? Ask building control</text><text x="60" y="878" font-size="16" fill="#6E645C">270 mm mineral wool and not squashing it: Which?. Light loads, vents and flues: council boarding guidance. Not to scale.</text></svg><figcaption>How to board a loft for storage: loft legs stand on the joists and lift the boards above the insulation, which stays at about 270 mm, with gaps left at the eaves so air keeps flowing.</figcaption></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Which? <a href="https://www.which.co.uk/reviews/insulation/article/how-to-buy-loft-insulation" target="_blank" rel="noopener">recommends 270 mm of mineral wool loft insulation</a> and warns that squashing it under boards reduces how well it works. It suggests raising the floor level so the full depth fits beneath, and loft legs are a common way to do this. North Tyneside Council&#8217;s <a href="https://www.northtyneside.gov.uk/boarding-out-loft-storage" target="_blank" rel="noopener">rules for tenants boarding out a loft</a> set three useful conditions: boarding should not compress the insulation, it should not block the ventilation the loft needs to avoid condensation, and it should leave flues alone. Its scheme also allows boarding only for light storage, such as suitcases and Christmas decorations.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you plan to use the loft as a room, the rules change. The Planning Portal explains that <a href="https://www.planningportal.co.uk/permission/common-projects/loft-conversion/is-building-regulations-approval-needed-for-a-loft-conversion" target="_blank" rel="noopener">building regulations approval is required to convert a loft into a liveable space</a>, and that existing joists are usually not designed for significant extra weight, so even boarding for storage can need approval. Check with your local council or building control before a big boarding job.</p>



